{{Term/Store|Stable Climate|Stable Climates|Series, TotK|plural}} are a recurring mechanic in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|TotK}}<ref name="TotK Yiga Clan Notebook"/> Stable Climates go unnamed in {{OoT}}, {{SS}}, {{BotW}}, and {{EoW}}.

==Overview==
==={{OoT|-}}===
{{Stub|OoT3D}}
In {{OoT}}, Stable Climates are areas that do not contain a [[Scorching Climate]]. Most of [[Hyrule]] is a Stable Climate, with the exception of the [[Death Mountain Crater]], [[Fire Temple]], and [[Fire Room]].

==={{SS|-}}===
{{Stub|SSHD}}
In {{SS}}, most of the [[Surface]] and the [[Sky]] consists of Stable Climates. The only place that does not contain a Stable Climate is the [[Volcano Summit]], which is instead a [[Scorching Climate]].

==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Stub|BotW}}
Stable Climates are parts of [[Hyrule]] that do not feature [[Extreme Temperature]]s, such as [[Freezing Climate]]s, [[Extremely Hot Zone]]s, and [[Scorching Climate]]s. When [[Link]] is in a Stable Climate, he will not take damage as he would in other environments.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Stub|TotK}}
In {{TotK}}, Stable Climates function the same as they do in {{BotW}}. [[Link]] is able to enter [[Cave]]s and [[Well]]s to avoid being damaged in hazardous environments.<ref name="TotK Tips and Tricks"/>

==={{EoW|-}}===
{{Stub|EoW}}
In {{EoW}}, Stable Climates are locations where [[Princess Zelda]] will not be damaged by a [[Freezing Climate]]. They are also places where she does not react to [[Heat]] or [[Scorching Climate]]s.

